	"description": [
		"Valuing nature raises significant philosophical and ethical issues. Students consider the nature of animal life, the character and control of pollution, the conflict between preservationism and conservationism, corporate responsibility for the eco-crisis, the use of economic categories to assess wilderness areas and endangered species, the conflict between eco-holism and individualism and the philosophy of wilderness management."
